    "axis": "aesthetics",
    "evidence": "Strong cyber-editorial identity, disciplined cyan/red semantics, crisp borders, and consistent typography. Tablet is the most balanced. Desktop is top-heavy: the oversized headline dominates while the core diagram is tiny inside a large empty panel. Mobile preserves hierarchy but has awkward headline wrapping and dense microcopy. The global header feels cramped and visibly clips/truncates navigation at tablet/mobile widths; several labels are very low contrast.",
